          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            %strong Geometric stability theory
            is the principal part of the branch of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+theory"} model theory
            called
            = succeed "." do
              %strong
                %span.newWikiWord
                  geometric model theory
                  %a{:href => "/nlab/new/geometric+model+theory"} ?
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Boris+Zilber"} Boris Zilber
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ehud+Hrushovski"} Ehud Hrushovski
          %p
            Geometric stability theory has largely to do with the model-theoretic classification of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure+in+model+theory"} structures
            in terms of dimension-like quantities that can be axiomatized in terms of notions of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/combinatorial+geometry"} combinatorial geometry
            such as
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/matroid"} matroid
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+spaces"} vector spaces
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraically+closed+fields"} algebraically closed fields
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+geometry"} algebro-geometric
            flavor (e.g., Morley rank as a generalization of Krull dimension).
          %p Such a structural geometric approach can make geometric stability theory an attractive key of entry into modern model theory for those mathematicians who are not already logicians.
          %h2#basic_concepts Basic concepts
          %p
            Perhaps the key axiomatic notions of geometric stability theory (which at the outset don’t seem particularly wedded to logic) are those of
            %em pregeometry
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %em geometry
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition Definition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              be a set. A
              %strong pregeometry
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closure+operator"} closure operator
              (i.e., a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad"} monad
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi cl
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi P
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi P
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} cl \colon P X \to P X
              on the
              = succeed ")," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/power+set"} power set
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  The monad
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi cl
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} cl
                  is
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finitary+functor"} finitary
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi P
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \in P X
                  and
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi a
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi cl
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi A
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \in cl(A)
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi A
                          %mn 0
                        %mo ⊆
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_0 \subseteq A
                  such that
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi a
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi cl
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi A
                            %mn 0
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \in cl(A_0)
              %li
                %p
                  (Exchange condition) If
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi A
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi P
                          %mi X
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \in P X
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi a
                          %mo ,
                          %mi b
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi X
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a,b \in X
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi a
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi cl
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi A
                          %mo ∪
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                          %mi b
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \in cl(A\cup\{b\})
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi cl
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \in cl(A)
                  or
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi b
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi cl
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi A
                          %mo ∪
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                          %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} a
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b \in cl(A \cup \{\a\})
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/matroid"} matroid
            %p
              A
              %strong geometry
              is a pregeometry such that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi cl
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ∅
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi ∅
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} cl(\emptyset) = \emptyset
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi cl
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} cl(\{x\}) = \{x\}
              for all
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in X
          .num_example
            %h6#examples Examples
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  Let
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                  be a
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+space"} vector space
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi cl
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} cl
                  be the monad on
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi P
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P X
                  whose algebras are vector subspaces of
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi X
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi cl
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} cl
                  is finitary (any subspace is the set-theoretic union of finite-dimensional subspaces), and the exchange condition is a classical fact about vector spaces related to the notion of independence. Thus
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi cl
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} cl
                  is a pregeometry.
              %li
                %p
                  Similarly, let
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                  be a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+space"} projective space
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi ℙ
                          %mi V
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{P}V
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi cl
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} cl
                  be the monad on
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi P
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P X
                  whose algebras are projective subspaces. Then
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi cl
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} cl
                  is a geometry (the closure of a point is a point). Any pregeometry
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi cl
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} cl
                  gives rise to a geometry in a similar way, in the sense that a pregeometry
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi cl
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} cl
                  induces a geometry on the image of the function
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi X
                          %mo →
                          %mi P
                          %mi X
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to P X
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi x
                          %mo ↦
                          %mi cl
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                          %mi x
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \mapsto cl(\{x\})
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#project"}
              %li
                %p
                  Let
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                  be an algebraically closed field; let
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi cl
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} cl
                  be the monad on
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi P
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P X
                  whose algebras are algebraically closed subfields. Then
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi cl
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} cl
                  is a pregeometry. That the exchange condition is satisfied is a classical result credited to Steinitz
                  %sup#fnref:1>
                    %a{:href => "#fn:1", :rel => "footnote"} 1
                  \.
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              Given a pregeometry
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mi cl
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X, cl)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi P
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \in P X
              is
              %strong independent
              if for all
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \in A
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                      %mo ∉
                      %mi cl
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mi a
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \notin cl(A - \{a\})
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              said to be a
              %strong basis
              for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi P
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y \in P X
              if
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Y
                      %mo ⊆
                      %mi cl
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y \subseteq cl(A)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
              have the same cardinality, called the
              %strong dimension
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              Given a pregeometry
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi cl
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X, cl)
              and a subset
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Y
                      %mo ⊆
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y \subseteq X
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi cl
                      %mi Y
                    %mo :
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} cl^Y: P(Y) \to P(Y)
              defined by the formula
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi cl
                      %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi cl
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∩
                    %mi Y
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} cl^Y(S) = cl(S) \cap Y.
            %p
              It is immediate that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ⊆
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \subseteq Y
              is independent in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi cl
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X, cl)
              iff it is independent in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Y
                      %mo ,
                      %msup
                        %mi cl
                        %mi Y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (Y, cl^Y)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi cl
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X, cl)
              iff it is a basis for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Y
                      %mo ,
                      %msup
                        %mi cl
                        %mi Y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (Y, cl^Y)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y \in P(X)
              has a well-defined dimension, we may assume without loss of generality that
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Y
                      %mo =
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y = X
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              has well-defined dimension was proven
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "nlab/show/matroid#welldefined"} here
          #project.num_remark
            %h6#remark_2 Remark
            %p
              There is a standard way of getting a geometry from a pregeometry
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mi cl
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X, cl)
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi cl
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ∅
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≠
                      %mi ∅
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} cl(\emptyset) \neq \emptyset
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              by
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo ′
                      %mo ≔
                      %mi X
                      %mo −
                      %mi cl
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ∅
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X' \coloneqq X - cl(\emptyset)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X'
              by
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∼
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \sim y
              if
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi cl
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
